tgs:Concept.SupernormalStimuli thinkr:relatesTo tgs:Concept.OneMarshmallowRewardCircuits ;
    skos:note "Nate's own real, recurring teaching concept: a modern invention or artifact that hijacks ancestral, evolved brain circuitry in a deleterious, maladaptive way relative to the environment that circuitry originally evolved for — vastly exceeding, in scale or intensity, anything the ancestral environment could have produced. Nate's own real, established example is money itself, particularly the US dollar; in a real, direct extension made during a conversation with Chuck Watson, he proposes nuclear weapons as an even larger supernormal stimulus, given their real, many-orders-of-magnitude greater destructive scale relative to any weapon available in humanity's tribal past."@en .

