tgs:Concept.MaximizingReturnsOnPower thinkr:relatesTo tgs:Concept.MaximumPowerPrinciple,
        tgs:Concept.MetabolicHierarchyOfTheSuperorganism,
        tgs:Concept.PowerVersusLife,
        tgs:Persona.DanielSchmachtenberger .

tgs:Concept.OneMarshmallowRewardCircuits thinkr:relatesTo tgs:Concept.DopamineHijackedCulture,
        tgs:Concept.RichInSocialCapital,
        tgs:Concept.SupernormalStimuli,
        tgs:Persona.DanielSchmachtenberger ;
    skos:note "Daniel Schmachtenberger's framing (Bend Not Break Part 3, TGS_31), after the marshmallow experiment, of how a market economy exploits evolved reward. In evolutionary settings, rewards came only with evolutionarily relevant work and with the deeper nourishment they were bound to. Supply-side incentives strip the reward from both: fast food delivers salt, fat and sugar without fiber or micronutrients (people dying of obesity are also micronutrient-starved, so the hunger deepens); porn delivers sexual reward without intimacy; social media delivers connection without the conflict-and-repair of real friendship. These are 'pseudosatisfiers.' Two-marshmallow circuits involve self-application and delayed, healthier gratification. The same split applies to understanding: quick certainty is a one-marshmallow reward (tgs:Concept.PrematureCertainty), and psychedelics can be 'one-marshmallows to spirituality.'"@en .

